          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A construction (
            %a{:href => "#UFP13"}> UFP13, Sec. 11.3
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive-inductive+type"} higher inductive-inductive type
          %p
            As opposed to the “naive”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+type"} quotient type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+Cauchy+sequences"} regular Cauchy sequences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            (i.e. the quotient type of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoid"} setoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bishop+set"} Bishop set
            by which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            are traditionally modeled in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+analysis"} constructive analysis
